## Notes

- All steps run non-interactively (no user input required)
- Uses local backends by default (Pulumi local, Terraform local)
- Generated code follows Planton conventions
- Both IaC implementations are at 100% behavioral parity (Parity Mandate + Phase 6b gate); any divergence is documented inline with `PARITY-EXCEPTION:`
- All documentation is substantial and production-ready
- Component is immediately usable after forge completes

## Success Criteria

After forge completes, the component should have:

✅ All 4 proto files with validations
✅ **Every CEL message is user-facing quality** (clear, actionable, empathetic -- see rule `002-spec-validate`, "VALIDATION MESSAGE QUALITY")
✅ **Every secret-bearing field annotated `(sensitive)`; every look-alike non-secret exempted with `sensitive_exempt_reason`** (see the Secret-by-default section)
✅ **`planton secret-coverage --check` passes** (no unannotated secret-looking field)
✅ Generated .pb.go stubs
✅ spec_test.go with validation tests
✅ **Component tests execute and pass** (validates buf.validate rules)
✅ Registered in cloud_resource_kind.proto
✅ Complete user-facing documentation (component-root README.md)
✅ Component-root `e2e/manifest.yaml` -- complete, protovalidate-valid, embedded as the reference Example and deployed by the E2E framework
✅ Pulumi module that compiles and works
✅ **Pulumi entrypoint at canonical root** (`iac/pulumi/main.go` is `package main`; no `main/` or `entrypoint/` subdir)
